module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.CompactObjects.ExtensionByZeroUnitAtTerminal
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ExtensionByZeroSubcomplexOnASite

/-!
# The span subcomplex over a final object is generated by a finite free module

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site, let `P` be a cochain complex of sheaves of `O`-modules whose terms
are presented as sums of extensions by zero of structure sheaves of slices, and let `S` be a
finite set of marked generators over an object `W`, closed under the differential. Each term of
the subcomplex of `P` spanned by `S` is the image of a finite sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W`
(`Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.epi_factorThruImage_gMap`). **When `W` is a final object of
`C` that finite sum is a finite free `O`-module**, because `j_{W!}O_W ≅ O` there
(`Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZero.extensionByZeroUnitIsoUnitOfTerminal`), so each term of the
subcomplex is a quotient of `O^{⊕r}`.

This is the last step of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FPV]: having built the finitely generated
subcomplex `K^•` whose terms in degrees `≥ m` are those of a strictly perfect complex `E^•`, the
source writes *"By construction we can choose an `r ≥ 0` and a surjection
`O^{⊕r} → K^{m-1}`"*, so that `(O^{⊕r} → E^m → E^{m+1} → …)` is strictly perfect. That reading
is available only because of the source's reduction *"we may assume `C` has a final object `X`"*,
under which the marked generators are global sections and `j_{X!}O_X = O`; at an arbitrary object
`j_{W!}O_W` is not a direct summand of a finite free `O`-module and no such surjection exists.
The reduction is realized by passing to the slice `C/W`, whose final object is `Over.mk (𝟙 W)`.

Nothing below is a clause of a tag; these are steps of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FPV], so no
`@[stacks …]` attribute is attached.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.extUnitIsoUnitOfTerminal`: `j_{W!}O_W ≅ O` for a final `W`,
  at the spelling in which the span construction writes the extension by zero.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.isIso_srcObjToFree`: the sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W` indexed
  by the generators of a given degree is a finite free module, over a final `W`.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.exists_epi_from_free`: **each term of the span subcomplex is
  a quotient of `O^{⊕r}`**, over a final `W`.

## Implementation notes

**Why a final object and not a subterminal one.**
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ExtensionByZero.isIso_extensionByZeroAdjunction_unit` identifies
`j_W^* j_{W!}O_W` with `O_W` for a subterminal `W`, which is what makes a copy of `j_{W!}O_W`
*restrict* to a copy of the structure sheaf; that is a statement on the slice and does not identify
`j_{W!}O_W` with `O` on `C`. What does is corepresentability: for a final `W` both `j_{W!}O_W` and
`O` corepresent the sections over `W`, which is
`Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZero.extensionByZeroUnitIsoUnitOfTerminal`, and that is the identification
used here. The subterminality obstruction recorded in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Modules/ExtensionByZeroSubcomplexOnASite.lean` is therefore
real at an arbitrary object and absent at a final one, which is the only case the induction of
[Stacks, Tag 0FPV] needs.

**Why only the epimorphism.** The second obstruction recorded there — that
`Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.gMap` need not be a monomorphism, since two marked generators
sharing an index name two sections of one summand with no independence between them — is not an
obstruction here. What the source asks for is a *surjection* `O^{⊕r} → K^{m-1}`, and
`Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.epi_factorThruImage_gMap` provides the epimorphism onto the
image unconditionally; monomorphy of `gMap` would be needed only to identify the image with the
free module itself, which the source never claims.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G1V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G1V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan

attribute [local instance] Abelian.hasFiniteBiproducts

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  (O : Sheaf J RingCat.{u})

/-- **The extension by zero of the structure sheaf of a slice over a final object is the
structure sheaf**, at the spelling `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.extUnit` uses. Both objects
corepresent the sections over the object, by [Stacks, Tag 0G1V] and by
`Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZero.unitHomEquivOfTerminal`. -/
def extUnitIsoUnitOfTerminal {W : C} (hW : IsTerminal W) :
    extUnit O W ≅ SheafOfModules.unit O :=
  Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZero.extensionByZeroUnitIsoUnitOfTerminal J O W hW

variable (P : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} O) ℤ) {I : ℤ → Type u} (U : ∀ n, I n → C)
  (ιP : ∀ n α, extUnit O (U n α) ⟶ P.X n)

/-- The comparison of the sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W` indexed by the marked generators of degree
`n` with the finite free module on the same index set, over a final `W`. -/
def srcObjIsoFree {W : C} (hW : IsTerminal W) (S : Finset (MarkedT U W)) (n : ℤ) :
    srcObj O U S n ≅ ⨁ fun _ : Fin (fibT U S n).card => SheafOfModules.unit O :=
  biproduct.mapIso fun _ => extUnitIsoUnitOfTerminal O hW

variable {O P U ιP}

variable {W : C} {S : Finset (MarkedT U W)}
  (hd : ∀ n, ∀ g ∈ fibT U S n,
    InSpan O (U (n + 1)) (cofanTerm O P U ιP (n + 1)) (fibT U S (n + 1))
      ((P.d n (n + 1)).val.app (op W) (elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) g)))

/-- **Each term of the span subcomplex is a quotient of a finite free `O`-module**, over a final
object `W`: the factorization of `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.gMap` through its image is an
epimorphism out of a sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W`, and each of those copies is `O`.

The rank is the number of marked generators of the degree in question, so it is finite because
`S` is. -/
theorem exists_epi_from_free (hW : IsTerminal W) (n : ℤ) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (q : (⨁ fun _ : Fin r => SheafOfModules.unit O) ⟶ (subcomplex hd).X n), Epi q :=
  ⟨(fibT U S n).card,
    (srcObjIsoFree O U hW S n).inv ≫ factorThruImage (gMap O P U ιP S n),
    @epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ inferInstance _
      (epi_factorThruImage_gMap (O := O) (P := P) (U := U) (ιP := ιP) (S := S) n)⟩

end Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan

end
